  "text": "The last boat is alongside. Mara still needs to help the passengers ashore.\n\nJo’s rolling projector, which shows the paper story’s pictures on a screen.\n\nBrightness that makes things visible; here, daylight or the lanterns’ glow.\n\nWater still comes through the opening. Move the same tile to cover the gap.\n\nThe passengers are safely ashore. Mara and Sol have arrived at the garden.\n\nYou direct the repair. Choose a position on the bird, then place the tape.\n\nThis shows the plan you are trying. Previewing does not tell your friends.\n\nDrag to guide the seed boat through the channel to Grandma’s blue landing.\n\nDrag to move · Release to place · Click a deck to walk · Escape to cancel\n\nPlace a section against the bank where the two sections can reach across.\n\nMove the sections farther from the seed boat’s route before joining them.\n\nRina moves her flour sacks away from the water dripping through the roof.\n\nLoop, a small cream and teal rolling projector with one large round lens.\n\nThe flour is dry. Rina can explain how to make dough and shape the bread.\n\nYour microphone is off. Choose Start listening when you're ready to read.\n\nThe whole story is playing. Its pictures and words advance automatically.\n\nWhy do you think the boy pulled the bird closer when Mara reached for it?\n\nChoose a tape position on the bird. Place the strip to see what it holds.\n\nForms of be: they describe what someone or something is like or is doing.\n\nMara is working at the usual time. Change the time or choose Pip to read.\n\nListening leaves every choice open. Select the reply you want Pip to use.\n\nThe lantern flowers around the planting circle hold the garden’s stories.\n\nThe seed rests in the prepared spot. It still needs its covering of soil.",
